TheBar native AmigaOS 3 integration
=================================

The source is pinned to the upstream 26.22 release in the TheBar git
submodule. COPYING contains its LGPL 2.1-or-later license. The release's
Source.tar.gz includes that checkout and the native build adapters.

Built components:
  TheBar.mcc       toolbar group
  TheBarVirt.mcc   toolbar in a virtual group
  TheButton.mcc    individual toolbar button
  TheBar.mcp       preferences page
  Toolbar.mcc      upstream compatibility wrapper for the older Toolbar API

All five are built for the 68000 with software floating point and are
loaded on demand. AmigaOS 3.0 or newer is required. Installer offers each
component under LIBS:MUI using its own version number, and separately
offers the available translations under LOCALE:Catalogs.

Native adaptations leave the pinned source checkout unchanged:
  - Reuse upstream OS3 source lists with an out-of-tree GCC/libnix build.
  - Supply bounded formatting, string and superclass varargs helpers.
  - Use the native NewObject entry point for open-ended BOOPSI macros.
  - Correct three preference-spec delimiter comparisons in generated
    copies of backgroundadjust.c and penadjust.c. The preparation step
    checks the original expressions and stops if upstream changes them.

Examples/TheBarDemo uses all four object classes with text buttons and
requires no image files. Run it normally for an interactive window, or
run "TheBarDemo CHECK" from a Shell for three brief open/close cycles.
It allocates a 64 KiB stack when the Shell stack is smaller. Its source
and public TheBar/Toolbar headers are included in SDK.

The Toolbar wrapper implements the older Toolbar interface using TheBar;
it is not a separate copy of the original Toolbar implementation. This
build does not claim every optional RTG effect or application-specific
Toolbar usage has been exercised.
